code-review engine (high), U3 round 1, branch 2026-09-26-mise-lock-honoured (develop...HEAD = a9f23b92..d0665861)

1. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/mise:36 — The plan's goal ('a lockfile is written only when none exists or under --upgrade') is not enforced: `mise run` installs missing tools before the task body runs, with `lockfile = true` and no `locked` in dev, so it resolves and writes lock entries itself. The find/mise lock branch never runs in practice. Scenario: scratch gate shows locks written by mise run's own auto-install; a developer adding a tool to mise.dev.toml and running plain setup gets it resolved to latest and written into mise.dev.lock without --upgrade. Fix: locked = true for dev too, or MISE_LOCKED=1 / task.run_auto_install = false for setup tasks.
2. .config/mise/tasks/setup/mise:60 — The removed unconditional `mise lock` plus `MISE_ENV=ci mise lock` gave every tool a URL for each platform in lockfile_platforms (linux-x64 for CI). Nothing replaces it on a plain run, so a tool locked by a plain install may carry only the host platform's URL. The .config/mise.toml comment at lines 8-14 names this failure; the only repair is now --upgrade, which bumps every other tool.
3. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise.toml:59 — The pack has no lockfile_platforms setting, and mise lock --bump falls back to the platforms already in the lockfile. If the first lockfile only has the developer's platform, every later --upgrade keeps it that way and CI's locked = true fails on linux.
4. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-gate/dprint/skills/dprint/SKILL.md:101 — Says the dprint update runs 'from setup:mise --upgrade only — never from a plain setup:mise, and never from setup:all, which passes no flag'. Now false. The file is in no unit's Owns.
5. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/mise:36 — find -name 'mise*.lock' treats any single lockfile (incl. gitignored mise.local.lock, or only mise.lock) as 'lockfiles exist', so missing committed lockfiles (mise.dev.lock) are never created by this branch. Should test each expected lockfile stem.
6. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/mise:23 — have_task parses `mise tasks` without --hidden; the pack hides every setup:* task, so a linter pack's hidden setup:lint is never found. Under pipefail, grep -qx exiting early can SIGPIPE awk.
7. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/mise:49 — The base MISE_ENV='' pass repeats work: every per-env pass re-locks mise.lock; dev,test re-bumps mise.dev.lock. Four network re-resolutions of mise.lock; any fetch failure aborts.
8. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/mise:53 — Env layering hardcoded as one special case (test → dev,test); any other layered env file (mise.e2e.toml) is locked without its base.
9. .config/mise/tasks/setup/all:87 — This repo's setup:all forwards --upgrade only to setup:mise, not the member loop, and uses an if/else rather than the pack's UPGRADE_ARGS array (recorded as G1, not fixed).
10. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/all:45 — Commit 16c74a5a changes plugin behaviour without the docs in the same commit; docs deferred to U4 in wave 3 (CLAUDE.md 'Docs ship with the change').
